vkd3d-proton: report the missing transform feedback once, not per command list

On a Vulkan device without transform feedback (MoltenVK), SOSetTargets
printed a FIXME on every call, and the D3D12 runtime clears the stream-output
targets on every command list reset -- one message a frame.  Written to a
console stderr that cost ~7 ms a frame: a tessellated D3D12 scene through the
AnyOS D3D12 UMD ran at 43 fps from a console and 95 fps with stderr
discarded.  The message is now FIXME_ONCE.

--- a/libs/vkd3d/command.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/command.c
@@ -15252,7 +15252,10 @@
 
     if (!list->device->vk_info.EXT_transform_feedback)
     {
-        FIXME("Transform feedback is not supported by Vulkan implementation.\n");
+        /* Once: the D3D12 runtime clears the SO targets on every command
+         * list reset, and a per-frame message cost ~7 ms a frame whenever
+         * stderr is a console. */
+        FIXME_ONCE("Transform feedback is not supported by Vulkan implementation.\n");
         return;
     }
 
